    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That seems a bit harsh on the urban areas. Isn't there a risk that by focusing all the \"efficient\" aid on the wealthy suburbs, we're just creating a cycle where the more diverse, lower-income neighborhoods get left behind and fall even further? If the goal is regional stability, shouldn't we consider that the urban areas actually have a higher need because they lack that same \"resilience\" you mentioned?",
